      "id": "5c113208-f9d4-489e-a0d6-97f7c34505f6",
      "type": "brief",
      "date": "2026-05-14T11:35:08.000Z",
      "title": "Full year 2026 earnings: EPS misses analyst expectations",
      "body": "Full year 2026 results: EPS: ₹45.96 (down from ₹58.00 in FY 2025). Revenue: ₹2.11t (up 22% from FY 2025). Net income: ₹267.0b (down 20% from FY 2025). Profit margin: 13% (down from 19% in FY 2025). The decrease in margin was driven by higher expenses. Revenue was in line with analyst estimates. Earnings per share (EPS) missed analyst estimates by 3.9%. Revenue is forecast to grow 11% p.a. on average during the next 3 years, compared to a 5.1% growth forecast for the Wireless Telecom industry in Asia. Over the last 3 years on average, earnings per share has increased by 55% per year but the company’s share price has only increased by 33% per year, which means it is significantly lagging earnings growth.",
      "keyDevTypeId": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "raw_subtype": "BriefActivity"
